 "about": "Each catalog product's priority food allergens, as Health Canada lists them (peanuts, tree nuts, sesame, milk, eggs, fish, crustaceans and molluscs, soy, wheat and triticale, mustard), with gluten sources and added sulphites, which Canadian labels must also name. Reviewed by hand from each product's name and description; these are demo products, so no real label was read. basis: 'what' the allergen is the product or what it names; 'recipe' the standard recipe for this kind of product contains it; 'typical' usual for this kind of product but not universal (a real label decides). Tags: dairy (milk), egg, fish, shellfish (crustaceans and molluscs), peanuts, tree_nuts, sesame, soy, gluten (wheat, triticale and other gluten sources), mustard, sulphites. A product with no tags has an empty object: it was reviewed and lists none.",
